# PROPOSAL ONLY (not applied). Read-only analysis, 18 Oct 2026, against the working tree at ~18:50.
# Owners: room_service screens.py (room_service owner), display page (display-page owner, vacant),
# stream_service media.py / diag.py / hud.py (stream_service owner).  All fields are additive: an old page,
# an old room_service or an old stream_service ignores them.
#
# PART A: the HUD/diag client mis-pick (task item 4)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bug 1  diag.py:111-125 client_stats() takes max(presented) over ALL media clients, ignoring role.  A plain
#        /display/<id> is role "kiosk" (src/pages/DisplayPage/index.tsx:66-70), so the owner's Brave tabs on PC22
#        are role=kiosk too [M W1: sessions_end.json, clients 172.28.240.1 (TV) and 127.0.0.1 (Brave) both
#        role "kiosk"].  The pick is the page with the bigger cumulative counter: whoever connected first or
#        reconnected least, not the TV.
# Bug 2  diag.py:117-123 keeps the dropped/s baseline on the SESSION (session._diag_prev), so when the pick flips
#        between two clients the rate is computed across two different counters (clipped to 0 or a spike).
# Bug 3  hud.py:271-278 takes the FIRST role in (None,"kiosk") client in connection order and breaks on it, so
#        a Brave tab that connected before the TV's (e.g. the TV page reloaded) is shown as "glass".
# Root   stream_service cannot tell the TV from another kiosk-role page.  room_service can: it drives exactly
#        one glass page per screen (screens.py _driven; glass_device = the TV's UA, pages.py:10-14, 62-66)
#        and every other page is a subscriber whose attach carries rejoin:true (screens.py:724-727).
#
# Fix: room_service marks the driven page's attach glass:true; the page echoes it (and its visibility) in its
#      media stats; stream_service picks glass first, never by presented count, and keeps rate baselines per
#      client.  No address heuristics (every socket arrives via the port proxy; owner: no hard-coded IPs).

