# PART B: measurement hooks to join glass stalls to server frames (task item 5) -- T3 in the diagnosis
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key fact: the frame id IS the media time.  renderer.py:853 writes tfdt = frame_id * frame_dur (90 kHz,
# fmp4.py:19) and the page already maps fid -> time as fid / fps (MseLivePlayer.ts:266).  So on the page:
#     fid_on_glass = Math.round(meta.mediaTime * fps)          (rVFC metadata, MseLivePlayer.ts:419-424)
#     fid_due      = Math.round(video.currentTime * fps)       (at a 'waiting' event)
# Keep frame ids on a fixed tick grid of the profile's fps (60) even after a 60->30 step (fid += 2), so this
# mapping never changes.
#
# Page (MseLivePlayer), all bounded, O(1) per frame:
#   per message:  rx_last_fid, rx_last_at (performance.now()), rx_hole when fid != last+1 (server drop-to-key
#                 or encoder skip): push {k:"hole", from, to}
#   per frame:    arrival margin = due time of that fid on the playhead clock - its arrival time; keep the
#                 per-second min (the single best "how close to a stall" number) and p50
#   per rVFC:     a presented-fid jump > 1 (missed frame on glass): push {k:"skip", from, to}
#   'waiting':    push {k:"stall", fid: fid_due, t, buf_ms, rx_fid: rx_last_fid, rx_age_ms: now - rx_last_at};
#                 on the next presented frame fill dur_ms
#   seeks:        gap skip / edge jump / kick each push {k:"gap"|"edge"|"kick", from_fid, to_fid}
#   clock:        answer the server's {"type":"ping","t":<server ns>} (a new TEXT type: MseLivePlayer.onMessage
#                 ignores unknown types today, :240-249, so old pages are safe) with pong {t, at: performance.now()}
#                 in the next stats; the server computes RTT and offset (min-RTT filter).  Powerline idle ping
#                 p50 2.4 ms / p99 8.7 ms (24 h soak, 13-14 Oct) => offset error ~1-4 ms.
#   stats (1 Hz, additive keys): fid_shown, rx_fid, margin_ms_min, margin_ms_p50, arr_gap_ms_p95/max,
#                 bytes, ev: [... at most 16 events since the last stats ...], pong
#   Do NOT add bits to the binary frame header: the page tests key as u8[1] !== 0 (:261), so a "repeat" flag
#   there would make every repeat look like a keyframe.
#
# stream_service (media.py MediaClient), per client, ring of 512 by fid:
#   t_queued (on_frame), t_handed (send_bytes start), t_drained (transport backlog back under WRITE_HIGH),
#   dropped (reason backlog|needs_key, backlog bytes), and ping/pong RTT + offset.  The engine already has
#   per-fid t_start / host_ms / t_written / encode_ms / repeat / held (renderer records).
#   Store the events and the ring OUTSIDE the session summary (summary() is polled ~1 Hz and stays small):
#   GET /api/sessions/<sid>/glass?since=<fid> (cached, read-only).
#
# Join (per page stall, by fid):  upstream  = packet out late vs its slot (t_written+encode vs deadline)
#                                 fan-out   = t_handed - packet_out large
#                                 network   = page arrival (offset-corrected) - t_handed large
#                                 decode/compositor = arrived with margin > 0 but rVFC skipped it
#                                 seek      = within 100 ms after an edge/gap/kick the page itself made
#                                 hole      = due fid inside a rx_hole (drop-to-key)
#   plus the freeze the page cannot see: server repeats and rate_div-held frames (renderer records), so the
#   "glass fps" line must be new pictures/s = sent - repeats - held, not the page's presented/s.
